      <p class="kicker">Lagom</p>
      <h1>One node, on purpose.</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The problem is a platform that is real Kubernetes, cheap enough to defend, and small
          enough that scarcity shows up in the jobs rather than in the overhead. A second machine
          was on the table. It is still in the design, as an edge node, and it is not where the
          platform runs.
        </p>
        <p>
          The decision is k3s on one Hetzner ARM node. The first node was a CAX11. The current one
          is a CAX21, because the work of the later milestone did not fit the smaller ceiling. Git
          is the source of truth for what the cluster runs. Argo CD reconciles the cluster to it.
          Secrets in Git are sealed. The public site, when it is published, is static files, so a
          visitor never reaches the node.
        </p>
        <p>
          The old quoted size of k3s was a story the machine did not confirm. The numbers below are
          the ones the architecture and the roadmap record. The exact monthly price of the current
          node is not among them. There is no second node for high availability, and that is
          written down as a choice. Terraform for the resources outside the cluster is still
          deferred. This site is not on the domain yet.
        </p>
      </div>
